# C/C++ and ESP-IDF — Coding Standards

<!-- cs: Standardy pro C/C++ firmware na ESP32 s ESP-IDF -->

## Language Standard

<!-- cs: Jazykový standard -->

- **C**: C11 (`-std=c11`), **C++**: C++17 (`-std=c++17`).
  <!-- cs: C: C11, C++: C++17. -->
- Prefer C where sufficient — C++ only for OOP abstractions (drivers, HAL layers).
  <!-- cs: Preferuj C tam kde postačuje — C++ jen pro OOP abstrakce (drivers, HAL vrstvy). -->
- ESP-IDF target: ESP32 / ESP32-S3 / ESP32-C3 — always specify in `CMakeLists.txt`.
  <!-- cs: ESP-IDF target vždy specifikuj v CMakeLists.txt. -->

## Docstrings — Doxygen Style

<!-- cs: Dokumentace — Doxygen -->

Every public function and class in `.h` / `.hpp` has a Doxygen comment:
<!-- cs: Každá veřejná funkce a třída v .h / .hpp má Doxygen komentář. -->

```c
/**
 * @brief Connect to the configured Wi-Fi network.
 *
 * Attempts connection up to MAX_RETRY_COUNT times with exponential back-off.
 *
 * @param[in]  config   Wi-Fi station configuration (SSID, password, channel).
 * @param[out] ip_info  Assigned IP address; valid only on ESP_OK.
 *
 * @return ESP_OK            Successfully connected and IP assigned.
 * @return ESP_ERR_TIMEOUT   All retries exhausted.
 * @return ESP_ERR_WIFI_*    Underlying Wi-Fi driver error.
 */
esp_err_t wifi_manager_connect(const wifi_config_t *config, esp_netif_ip_info_t *ip_info);
```

- Implementation files (`.c`/`.cpp`) may use shorter comments — details belong in `.h`.
  <!-- cs: Implementační soubory mohou mít stručnější komentáře — detaily patří do .h. -->

## Naming Conventions

<!-- cs: Pojmenování -->

| Type | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Functions (C) | `snake_case` | `wifi_connect()` |
| Macros and constants | `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` | `MAX_RETRY_COUNT` |
| Variables | `snake_case` | `retry_count` |
| Types (typedef) | `snake_case_t` | `wifi_config_t` |
| Classes (C++) | `PascalCase` | `WifiManager` |
| Files | `snake_case` | `wifi_manager.c` |
| ESP-IDF components | `lowercase` directory | `components/wifi_manager/` |

## Include Guards and Order

<!-- cs: Include guards a pořadí include souborů -->

```c
#pragma once   // preferred over classic include guards

// Include order in .c / .cpp:
#include "wifi_manager.h"    // own header first — reveals missing dependencies
#include <stdint.h>          // standard C library
#include <string.h>
#include "esp_log.h"         // ESP-IDF headers
#include "freertos/FreeRTOS.h"
#include "freertos/task.h"
```

## Error Handling — Mandatory

<!-- cs: ESP-IDF error handling — povinné -->

```c
// ✅ Always check esp_err_t return values
static const char *TAG = "wifi_manager";

esp_err_t ret = esp_wifi_connect();
if (ret != ESP_OK) {
    ESP_LOGE(TAG, "esp_wifi_connect failed: %s", esp_err_to_name(ret));
    return ret;
}

// ✅ Macro for repeated error-check pattern (define project-wide)
#define ESP_RETURN_ON_ERROR(x, tag, msg) do {               \
    esp_err_t err_ = (x);                                   \
    if (err_ != ESP_OK) {                                   \
        ESP_LOGE(tag, "%s: %s", msg, esp_err_to_name(err_)); \
        return err_;                                        \
    }                                                       \
} while(0)

ESP_RETURN_ON_ERROR(esp_wifi_init(&cfg), TAG, "wifi init failed");
```

## Logging — ESP-IDF Macros Only

<!-- cs: Logging — výhradně ESP-IDF makra -->

```c
static const char *TAG = "module_name";  // each module has its own TAG

ESP_LOGI(TAG, "Connected to %s (RSSI: %d dBm)", ssid, rssi);
ESP_LOGW(TAG, "Retry %d/%d", attempt, MAX_RETRIES);
ESP_LOGE(TAG, "Connection failed: %s", esp_err_to_name(ret));
ESP_LOGD(TAG, "Raw packet: %d bytes", len);  // debug level only

// ❌ Never printf() for firmware diagnostics
```

## Memory Management

<!-- cs: Správa paměti -->

```c
// ✅ Prefer static allocation (stack or static keyword)
static uint8_t rx_buffer[RX_BUFFER_SIZE];

// ✅ If heap — always check NULL and free
char *buf = malloc(size);
if (buf == NULL) {
    ESP_LOGE(TAG, "malloc failed, size=%zu", size);
    return ESP_ERR_NO_MEM;
}
// ... use ...
free(buf);

// ❌ Never malloc without NULL check
// ❌ No GC exists — every malloc must have a corresponding free
```

## FreeRTOS

<!-- cs: FreeRTOS -->

```c
// Task creation — always check return value
BaseType_t res = xTaskCreatePinnedToCore(
    wifi_task, "wifi_task", 4096, NULL, 5, &wifi_task_handle, APP_CPU_NUM
);
configASSERT(res == pdPASS);

SemaphoreHandle_t mutex = xSemaphoreCreateMutex();
configASSERT(mutex != NULL);

// ❌ Never busy-wait — always vTaskDelay or Event Group
while (!connected) {
    vTaskDelay(pdMS_TO_TICKS(100));  // ✅ yields CPU
}
```

## Defensive Programming

<!-- cs: Bezpečnost a defensive programming -->

```c
// Validate all inputs at function entry
void process_data(const uint8_t *data, size_t len) {
    if (data == NULL || len == 0 || len > MAX_PACKET_SIZE) {
        ESP_LOGE(TAG, "Invalid input: data=%p, len=%zu", data, len);
        return;
    }
}

snprintf(url, sizeof(url), "https://api.example.com/v1/%s", endpoint); // snprintf, not sprintf
configASSERT(handle != NULL);  // invariants — disabled in Release build
```

## OOP in C++ — RAII

<!-- cs: OOP v C++ — RAII a návrhové vzory -->

**RAII** — every resource (memory, mutex, handle) is owned by an object; destructor guarantees release:
<!-- cs: RAII — každý zdroj je vlastněn objektem; destruktor zaručuje uvolnění. -->

**Rule of Five** — if you define any of {destructor, copy constructor, copy assignment, move constructor, move assignment}, define all five explicitly:
<!-- cs: Rule of Five — pokud definuješ destruktor nebo jakýkoliv copy/move, definuj všech pět explicitně. -->

```cpp
// Pattern: RAII — FreeRTOS mutex guard (analogous to std::lock_guard)
class MutexGuard {
public:
    explicit MutexGuard(SemaphoreHandle_t mutex) : mutex_(mutex) {
        xSemaphoreTake(mutex_, portMAX_DELAY);
    }
    ~MutexGuard() { xSemaphoreGive(mutex_); }

    // Rule of Five: non-copyable, non-movable (owns exclusive FreeRTOS handle)
    MutexGuard(const MutexGuard&)            = delete;
    MutexGuard& operator=(const MutexGuard&) = delete;
    MutexGuard(MutexGuard&&)                 = delete;
    MutexGuard& operator=(MutexGuard&&)      = delete;

private:
    SemaphoreHandle_t mutex_;
};

void critical_section() {
    MutexGuard guard(shared_mutex_);  // acquired here
    // ... work ...
}                                      // released automatically on scope exit
```

**`std::optional`** — use for values that may be absent; avoids sentinel values (C++17, supported in ESP-IDF):
<!-- cs: std::optional — pro hodnoty, které mohou chybět; vyhýbá se sentinel hodnotám (C++17, podporováno v ESP-IDF). -->

```cpp
#include <optional>

std::optional<sensor_data_t> read_sensor() {
    if (!sensor_ready()) {
        return std::nullopt;  // explicit absence — no magic -1 or nullptr
    }
    return sensor_data_t{ .temperature = read_temp(), .humidity = read_hum() };
}

auto data = read_sensor();
if (data.has_value()) {
    ESP_LOGI(TAG, "Temp: %.1f", data->temperature);
}
```

## .gitignore — C/C++ and ESP-IDF-Specific Entries

<!-- cs: .gitignore — C/C++ a ESP-IDF-specific záznamy -->

Add these to the project `.gitignore` when C/C++ or ESP-IDF is used:
<!-- cs: Přidej toto do .gitignore při použití C/C++ nebo ESP-IDF: -->

```gitignore
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.d
build/
cmake-build-*/
CMakeFiles/
CMakeCache.txt
compile_commands.json
sdkconfig.old
dependencies.lock
managed_components/
```

## ESP-IDF Component Structure

<!-- cs: Struktura ESP-IDF komponenty -->

```
components/
└── wifi_manager/
    ├── CMakeLists.txt
    ├── include/
    │   └── wifi_manager.h    # Public API
    ├── wifi_manager.c
    └── README.md             # Component description, API, usage example
```

```cmake
idf_component_register(
    SRCS "wifi_manager.c"
    INCLUDE_DIRS "include"
    REQUIRES esp_wifi nvs_flash freertos
)
```
